"The customer-randomised test of the new dispatch rule showed treated orders arriving 10.4 minutes sooner and converting +4.4 points more often. Run for everyone, the simulator gives a gain of only 1.8 minutes and +0.7 points of conversion. The test overstated the delivery gain by 8.6 minutes because treated and control customers share couriers: the rule moved waiting from control orders to treated ones, and only the batching gain is real. A customer-randomised test cannot measure this change."
